.TH CAPTDUMP 1 "August 2026" "capt6000 1.0" "capt6000"
.SH NAME
captdump \- decode a capt6000 record stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B captdump
.RB [ \-o
.IR outdir ]
.I stream
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B captdump
reads a capt6000 intermediate record stream \(em the output of the
.B rastertolbp6000
filter \(em and prints the page parameters, the Hi\-SCoA parameters and a
per\-band decode summary in human readable form.
.PP
With
.BR \-o ,
every page is additionally decompressed back into a PBM image written as
.IR outdir /page\-NNN.pbm ,
so the raster the printer would receive can actually be looked at.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " outdir"
Write each decoded page as a PBM image into
.IR outdir .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 2 if no input file was given, and 1 on a read error
or if the file is not a capt6000 stream.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR captwire (1),
.BR captstat (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Viktor Hozhyi.  Part of capt6000,
.UR https://github.com/ViktorGozhiy/capt6000
.UE .
